{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-20750-r4613696","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Barbecue Sauce (Kansas City-style)","sourcePageId":20750,"sourceRevision":"4613696","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-01-26T02:28:00Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Barbecue%20Sauce%20(Kansas%20City-style)&oldid=4613696","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:40.533Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Gluten-free recipes","Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for barbecue sauce","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ketchup","Category:Recipes using liquid smoke","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using prepared mustard","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"0d2a3bc74567c2f6bb42c42fd806309a8297a47cad641b61ebba548c9319b5f1","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Sauce recipes|servings=8|time=20 minutes|difficulty=1|yield = 2 cups}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Sauce|Sauce]]\n\n'''Barbecue Sauce''' is a [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]] or [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]] based [[Cookbook:Sauce|sauce]] used on [[Cookbook:Meat|meats]]. Kansas City-style barbecue sauce is the most common version used in the [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|United States]]. It is tomato- or ketchup- based with sweet, sour and smoky elements. Barbecue sauce can be added to the meat before, during or after cooking. This version contains quite a bit of [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]], so it should be added near the end or after cooking the meat to avoid burning the sauce.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (235 [[Cookbook:mL|mL]]) [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n*6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] (90 mL) [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n*4 tablespoons (60 mL) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*3 tablespoons (45 mL) white [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]]\n*1 tablespoon (15 mL) plain prepared [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n*3 tablespoons (45 mL) finely minced yellow [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*4 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] (20 mL) bottled [[Cookbook:Liquid Smoke|liquid smoke]] flavor (hickory)\n*¼ teaspoon (1 mL) Louisiana-style [[Cookbook:Red Pepper|red pepper]] [[Cookbook:Sauce|sauce]]\n*½ cup (120 mL) [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*1 tablespoon (15 mL) [[Cookbook:Granulated Sugar|granulated sugar]]\n*1 teaspoon (5 mL) [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine all ingredients in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]].\n#Mix well.\n#[[Cookbook:Simmer|Simmer]] over low heat for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* This sauce tastes very close to commercial barbecue sauces such as Masterpiece and Bullseye.\n\n==Warnings==\n* Keep refrigerated\n* Add to meat near end or after cooking to avoid burning sauce because of sugar content.\n\n[[Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes for barbecue sauce]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using liquid smoke]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using prepared mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Barbecue Sauce (Kansas City-style)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup (235 mL) ketchup","sourceText":"1 cup (235 mL) ketchup","amountText":"1 cup (235 mL) ketchup","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"6 tablespoons (90 mL) Worcestershire sauce","sourceText":"6 tablespoons (90 mL) Worcestershire sauce","amountText":"6 tablespoons (90 mL) Worcestershire sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 tablespoons (60 mL) butter or margarine","sourceText":"4 tablespoons (60 mL) butter or margarine","amountText":"4 tablespoons (60 mL) butter or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) white vinegar","sourceText":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) white vinegar","amountText":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) white vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) plain prepared mustard","sourceText":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) plain prepared mustard","amountText":"1 tablespoon (15 mL) plain prepared mustard","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) finely minced yellow onion","sourceText":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) finely minced yellow onion","amountText":"3 tablespoons (45 mL) finely minced yellow onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"4 teaspoons (20 mL) bottled liquid smoke flavor (hickory)","sourceText":"4 teaspoons (20 mL) bottled liquid smoke flavor (hickory)","amountText":"4 teaspoons (20 mL) bottled liquid smoke flavor (hickory)","amount":null,"uni